# Good UI/UX
    Bootstrap, or another CSS framework, styling
    Make it look professional. This should feel like a real booking dashboard.
    Entire process must work in mobile, tablet, and desktop, from beginning to end
    A functional map using Leaflet displaying all hotel locations in the JSON file described

# JSON FILES
    HOTEL instructions
        Every hotel must have a unique id.
        When the user clicks a hotel on the map, only the rooms with the matching hotelId should appear.
        
        The hotel file must contain 12 hotel objects. 
        Each hotel object represents one hotel location in the chain.

        When the user clicks a hotel on the map, only the rooms with the matching hotelId should appear.

        Be sure to use images for rooms and hotels

        hotels.json stores the hotel locations and hotel details used for the Leaflet map and hotel information section.

        ROOM instructions
            Every room must have a hotelId that matches the 'owning' hotel id.
            
            The rooms file must contain 36 room objects.
            Each room object must belong to one hotel using the hotelId property
            With 12 hotels and 36 rooms, each hotel should have about 3 room options connected to it.

            rooms.json stores the room data used for the room catalog and booking cart.

# FUNCTIONAL HOTEL MAP
**Your map must be functional and clearly connected to the booking process**
**Your selected hotel must control which rooms appear on the page**
    User location is found and placed on the map using Geolocation // wont work at school

    All hotel locations are displayed on an interactive LeafletJS map
            clickable 
            custom hotel icon

    Clicking a hotel must bring up that hotel location for the user to book from

    The clicked hotel should 
            become the active hotel 
            populate the page with that location's room options and ONLY the selected hotel's rooms
            display Weather data for the selected hotel location
            have a popup
            become map focus ("clearly")

# FUNCTIONAL ROOM CATALOG
**Your room catalog must be populated dynamically from JSON**
    Rooms are (function) 
            populated from 'rooms' JSON file via fetch
            filterable
                via category chooser, drop down select box, or another filtering method 
            sortable
                by price, room type, max guests, rating, or another logical room category

    Rooms are (visual)
            displayed as cards 
            in grid, row, or masonry layout
            include:
                image, hotel name, room name, room type, number of beds, max guests, nightly cost, and availability status
                Book Room button (functional)
    
    Book Room button adds that room to the cart in the offcanvas menu 

# FUNCTIONAL OFFCANVAS BOOKING CART
**If the page is refreshed, items should still show in the cart**
**Your cart must store data in localStorage** 
    Use an Offcanvas for user to view
        choose one of: overlay, offcanvas, popover, or panel 
        shows rooms being booked 
        when open, rest of the catalog is hidden
    Cart functions
        Provide total (cost?) of rooms booked and a subtotal
        Items can be removed from the cart
        The cart can be emptied
    don't worry about dates - if a room is booked, its not available
    booking is reserved if added to cart - no timeout

# FUNCTIONAL BOOKING OR CHECKOUT SYSTEM
**Validate all form fields and provide meaningful user feedback**
    Create a checkout process to complete bookings
    Checkout should 
        collect:
            "meaningful information" such as
            customer name, email, phone, address, city, province or state, postal code, number of guests, and number of nights
        Show:
            order summary, includes: hotel selected, room booked, nights stayed, guests, subtotal, taxes, and final total
        
        Confirmation section or confirmation message after successful booking
 
# WEATHER AND PRICING LOGIC
    Weather data must affect your dashboard in a meaningful way
        adding weather icon or text satisfies this requirement
    Pricing logic is not needed
        Any pricing logic used must make sense and be displayed clearly to the user

